Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 10:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 17/23] Check the path of a restart file before deleting it

With -T, a group that restarts a failed transfer and then ends
without that file deletes the partial file of the earlier run under
the temp directory. A FILEINFO of the restarted group could first
replace a directory of that path with a symbolic link, and the
deletion then removed a file outside the temp directory. Leave the
file alone when a directory in its path is a symbolic link.
---
 client_common.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/client_common.c b/client_common.c
index f89c14d..2a21c5b 100644
--- a/client_common.c
+++ b/client_common.c
@@ -506,6 +506,11 @@ void file_cleanup(struct group_list_t *group, int abort_session)
                 glog0(group,"Max pathname length exceeded: %s%c_group_%08X%c%s",
                             tempdir, PATH_SEP, group->group_id, PATH_SEP,
                             group->restartinfo->name);
+            } else if (link_in_path(filepath,
+                    len - strlen(group->restartinfo->name) - 1)) {
+                // A later FILEINFO can replace a directory of the path.
+                glog0(group, "Leaving %s: a directory in its path is a "
+                             "symbolic link", filepath);
             } else {
                 unlink(filepath);
             }
